            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis of Mesenteric Ectopic Pancreas by Secretin-Enhanced Magnetic Resonance Cholangiopancreatography.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RCT.0000000000000665</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ectopic pancreas (EP) is defined as pancreatic tissue found outside its usual anatomical position, with no ductal or vascular communication with the native pancreas.We report the case of a 59-year-old woman with a mesenteric jejunal EP initially suspected on computed tomography and confirmed by secretin-enhanced magnetic resonance cholangiopancreatography.Mesenteric EP is a very rare finding with nonspecific clinical presentation, so that, classic radiological findings have not been well described previously.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
